# Environment Variables — متغيرات البيئة

Copy this file to `.env.local` (development) or configure in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables (production).

## MONGODB_URI (required)

Connection string for the MongoDB database.

- Local development: `mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/masjed`
- Production (Atlas): `mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/masjed?retryWrites=true&w=majority`

The last path segment (`masjed`) is the database name.

## JWT_SECRET (required in production)

Secret used to sign session tokens (HS256). Sessions invalidate if this changes.

Generate a strong value:

```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
```

Development fallback exists but **must not** be used in production.

## ENABLE_QUICK_LOGIN (optional)

Dev/demo shortcut `POST /api/auth/quick-login` that enters the project
without typing credentials. Enabled by default outside production,
disabled in production unless set to `true`.

```bash
ENABLE_QUICK_LOGIN=true   # allow quick login in production (demo only)
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_QUICK_LOGIN=true  # show the quick-login button in production
```

Optional custom demo account (used only when no teacher exists yet):

```bash
QUICK_LOGIN_EMAIL=admin@local.test
QUICK_LOGIN_PASSWORD=Admin1234
```

---

## Example / مثال

```bash
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/masjed
JWT_SECRET=your-generated-random-string-here
```
